{"timestamp": 1779426037.2565916, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 21, "data": {"caller": "player_1", "reason": "Bob reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "weapons", "victim_name": "Eve"}, {"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Alice"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779426037.2574115, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 21, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779426044.5825982, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 21, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I found Eve's body in weapons just now. My route was upper engine, oxygen, back to upper engine, then through medbay, electrical, security, and finally weapons where I found her. I saw Charlie early in the round around oxygen and upper engine, but I haven't seen anyone recently on the right side of the map. Did anyone pass by weapons or security? Also, check if anyone saw anything near medbay since I passed through there earlier."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426063.9121664, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 21, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I can add some timing: I started electrical/security side, and I did see Eve go from electrical through security toward weapons pretty early. I passed weapons briefly after that and Eve was alive there. Then I went cafeteria \u2192 medbay, where I saw Alice alive, and after that I went upper engine \u2192 lower engine \u2192 storage. Frank was with me in storage when the report happened, so I definitely wasn\u2019t near weapons recently.\n\nBob, your route ending security into weapons is exactly where Eve died, so I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s you, but timing matters a lot here. Charlie being around oxygen/upper engine early also lines up with the left side near where Alice might\u2019ve been after medbay. We need Frank/Charlie\u2019s routes."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426076.550096, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 21, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I started out on the top left. My route was oxygen, upper engine, lower engine, storage, and then I ended up in navigation. I can confirm I saw Bob early on in oxygen and upper engine, but after that I didn't cross paths with anyone. \n\nDiana, I didn't see you or Frank in storage, so I must have passed through before you two got there. \n\nLooking at the routes, Bob is placing himself in medbay (where Diana last saw Alice alive) and in weapons (where Eve was found dead). That gives him a lot of opportunity for both kills. But since it's just 4 of us left and 1 duck, we need to be careful\u2014a wrong vote could cost us the game if the duck gets another kill. Let's see what Frank says to confirm Diana's alibi in storage. If we aren't 100% sure, we might want to skip, but Bob is definitely my top suspect right now based on positioning."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426114.4122233, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 21, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I can vouch for Diana, she was definitely with me in Storage when the meeting was called. My route was Cafeteria -> Medbay -> Cafeteria -> Oxygen -> Upper Engine -> Lower Engine -> Storage. I actually didn't see anyone at all until I bumped into Diana at the very end. I also didn't see Alice when I was in Medbay early on, so she must have gone there after I had already left.\n\nSince Diana and I were in Storage on the bottom of the map, there's no way either of us killed Eve over in Weapons right before the report. That means the Duck has to be either Bob or Charlie. Bob, your route puts you right through Medbay (where Alice might be) and into Weapons (where you found Eve), which looks pretty bad. However, Charlie ending up in Navigation means he was also on that side of the map and could have easily accessed Weapons through Security. \n\nHere's the most important thing: there are only 4 of us left and 1 Duck. If we vote wrong right now, it's game over as soon as the Duck gets their next cooldown. It's too risky to guess between Bob and Charlie without a smoking gun. We need to skip this vote. \n\nDiana, let's stick together like glue this next round. Bob and Charlie, you two should probably buddy up as well. If anyone breaks from their pair or we find another body, we'll know exactly who to vote for. I'm skipping.\n\n=== VOTE ===\nskip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779426125.7744246, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 21, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "skip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779426148.0996704, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 21, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I agree with Frank that the safest mechanical play is probably skip, but I don\u2019t want us to ignore the pattern here.\n\nMy hard info is: Eve went electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons, and I saw her alive in weapons earlier. Alice was alive in medbay when I passed through. After that I went left side and ended in storage with Frank, so Frank and I are pretty paired for the end timing.\n\nThat leaves Bob and Charlie as the realistic suspects. Charlie says he ended navigation, which is near weapons, so I\u2019m not clearing him. But Bob\u2019s route is the one that literally includes medbay and then security/weapons, plus he\u2019s the reporter on Eve. That\u2019s a lot of overlap with both death areas.\n\nI\u2019m okay skipping if that\u2019s where the group is, but next round we need strict pairs. Frank, I\u2019ll stick with you. Bob and Charlie should stay together, and if one of them dies or separates, we\u2019ll have the answer."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426157.8055632, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 21, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "skip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779426171.5036197, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 21, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I'm not sure why my thoughts from earlier seemed to echo, but to finalize everything before we vote: Diana is 100% cleared by me. We were together in storage on the complete opposite side of the map from where Eve was found in Weapons. \n\nThat means we have a 50/50 coin flip between Bob and Charlie. Bob's route puts him directly through both kill zones (Medbay and Weapons), making him the prime suspect. However, Charlie ended up in Navigation, which is just one room away from Weapons, so he had the opportunity as well.\n\nWith only 4 of us left and 1 Duck, a wrong vote means we lose instantly when the Duck's cooldown resets. We cannot risk a 50/50 guess right now. \n\nWe skip this. Diana, you and I are glued together for the rest of the game. Bob and Charlie, you two need to buddy up. If anyone separates from their partner, or if one of you dies, the remaining person is getting voted out. Play safe.\n\nskip"}}
